0 Batima - one brick, alone in a white studio (A3-S02)
0 Name: batima.ldr
0 Author: spex project (hand-authored placement data; not sourced from an official ldraw.org models/ release)
0 // The Batima system, Le Batima Soc., FR 588985, c. 1924. The shot's
0 // lower third carries that number and not BE 311029 / 1923, which could
0 // not be confirmed.
0 //
0 // The geometry is deliberately the plainest thing in the piece: ONE
0 // Brick 2 x 4 (3001.dat), the part every later claim is about. A
0 // reconstruction of the Batima brick's own profile would be a drawing
0 // of a patent, and this shot already has the drawing - it is an overlay,
0 // not geometry. What the picture has to carry is that the object is
0 // ordinary.
0 //
0 // Colour 15 (White) for all three patent bricks - Batima, Kiddicraft and
0 // 1949 - because they ARE the same object, and that is the whole content
0 // of Interlego v Tyco. Giving them three colours would be an editorial
0 // claim the piece spends three shots arguing against. The lower thirds
0 // do the distinguishing.
0 //
0 // Stage position: x = 20000 LDU (1000 studs), the third station of the
0 // world plate after Act II's coin at 800. Instance translations in a
0 // mesh bundle are i16 LDU, so the whole piece must stay inside
0 // +/-32767 LDU; Act III ends at 23600 and leaves Act IV the rest.
0 //
0 // Brick 2 x 4 is 24 LDU tall and its origin is the centre of its
0 // footprint, so a part sitting on the ground plane is translated to
0 // y = -24 in LDraw's +Y-down frame.
1 15 20000 -24 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3001.dat
